  "feature": "aitp-a2a-agent-card",
  "$comment": "The Agent Card is an A2A 1.0.0 AgentCard (JSON names as in the A2A specification, https://a2a-protocol.org/latest/specification/). `input.agent_card` is the Card as fetched; `input.selected_interface_url` is the AgentInterface the client intends to call; `input.manifest` is the Manifest fetched from the Card's `params.manifestUrl` (inner body; placeholders resolve as for man-*), or `input.manifest_fetch` records a fetch outcome. The runner MUST NOT fetch anything.",
  "description": "The Card's `params.aid` uses the algorithm-tagged form `aid:pubkey:ed25519:<key>` while agent B's Manifest uses the legacy untagged form of the same Ed25519 key. RFC-AITP-0001 §5.3 makes the two forms equal for trust decisions, and RFC-AITP-0014 §4.2 step 4 compares by algorithm and key, so the binding succeeds.",
  "tags": [
    "success",
    "a2a",
    "agent-card",
    "aid-equivalence"
  ],
